WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.130
Speaker 1: Let's talk a little bit about we
are just asking questions.

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.160
We are just asking questions.

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.540
I'm going to play you a clip from CNN of James
Colmer being interviewed by Kaitlan Collins

00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:17.130
and confronted about a conspiracy theory he
floated about the Chinese balloon.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.130
Take a look at this.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.380
Speaker 6: One thing you said as we were learning
about this balloon and tracking it, you asked

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:23.710
on Fox News, is it bioweapons in that balloon?

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:25.260
Did that balloon take off from Wuhan?

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:26.480
We don't know anything about it.

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.440
But you don't have any evidence that this.

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:29.440
No.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:30.440
Speaker 7: I asked the question.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.759
I mean, what is in the balloon?

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:38.829
This is something that we believe the White
House should have advised us.

00:00:38.829 --> 00:00:42.280
So they should have had a briefing to tell
us what this was.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.210
I think back home in Kentucky, this is all
anybody talks about was this flu.

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.210
Everyone was concerned.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:49.450
Speaker 1: In Kentucky, it was all balloon
24 seven.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:51.410
Speaker 7: No one trusts China.

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.820
They know China is an adversary.

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:58.300
My concern was the military had no idea anything
about the balloon.

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.590
What was in the balloon?

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:01.670
Was it a spy balloon?

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.760
Was it a weather balloon like China said?

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:08.070
You know, what exactly did the did the US
military know about this?

00:01:08.070 --> 00:01:10.299
What did our intelligence know about this?

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:14.900
Did they know it was even in airspace before
it got in the Alaska airspace?

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.790
So, you know, it's just a lot of questions.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:19.030
And that's just one of the questions.

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.310
Just for all we know, it could have bioweapons.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.310
They could be testing.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:24.930
No, no, I didn't ask the question, but.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:29.790
Speaker 1: He's just asking questions, sort
of like I could say.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:36.140
Is James Colmer, a pedophile bank robber who
secretly spends his time producing child porn?

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.250
Why hasn't anyone investigated it?

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.580
Why won't anyone investigate it?

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:43.299
Well, David, because there's no evidence of
that.

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:48.340
I'm just asking questions, as a phrase has
become a really common defense for people

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:50.630
who promote conspiracy theories.

00:01:50.630 --> 00:01:55.990
But it's actually a dangerous weaponization
of free speech, because the idea behind I'm

00:01:55.990 --> 00:02:00.710
just asking questions is I'm seeking information.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:03.200
I'm not promoting anything false by asking
a question.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.200
How could I?

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:05.200
It's just a question.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.209
I'm asking a question because I seek information.

00:02:08.209 --> 00:02:12.580
But that's of course, not the case when it
comes to a lot of these conspiracy theories.

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:19.390
The people who are just asking questions are
asking questions as a way to promote false,

00:02:19.390 --> 00:02:24.550
baseless, sometimes harmful ideas without
having to take the responsibility for the

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.750
consequences of floating those ideas.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.610
Someone might say, I'm just asking questions.

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:31.459
Have you ever considered that the moon landing
was faked?

00:02:31.459 --> 00:02:32.920
Why haven't you considered it?

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.920
Whatever.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:40.170
And when you look at the intent of that, it
implies there is reason to support the conspiracy

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.670
theory when in fact there's overwhelming evidence
to show actually the moon landing was real.

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:50.540
And the problem with this type of rhetoric
is that it lets the false information spread

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.069
without being challenged, because at the end
of the day, what's wrong with asking a question?

00:02:54.069 --> 00:03:00.370
And it also creates a false equivalency between
here are the established facts and here are

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.720
just these are questions and they're just
as valid.

00:03:02.720 --> 00:03:07.360
Well, actually there are questions with the
intent to promote a conspiracy theory.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:13.319
And when someone says I'm just asking questions,
we can evaluate their intention.

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:16.740
Why is it that they are asking this question
and not a different one?

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.770
Why is Colmer asking murmur?

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:21.020
He doesn't have evidence for any of this stuff.

00:03:21.020 --> 00:03:22.931
Why is he asking Were there what?

00:03:22.931 --> 00:03:24.070
What did he say?

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.670
Were there bioweapons versus were there Tootsie
Rolls?

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.670
Right.

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:29.140
Both would just be questions.

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:31.120
No evidence for either.

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.709
Why is he asking one but not the other?

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:34.560
Well, you have to go and look at his intent.

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:40.150
And the intent, of course, is to show exactly
this type of concern about the Biden administration.

